This violates He2025: a pinned input can return a cached result from a DIFFERENT tier than the pin specifies.

**Fix:** Move the pinned-tier execution block (lines 277-285) ABOVE the cache check block (lines 256-272). The tier-pin read at lines 249-251 stays where it is. The execution of the pinned tier moves up:

